# Freeze localisation: the round asks where SpringBoard and backboardd sit while the panel stops
# changing, so the drags are not the subject here. Two framewatch runs:
#
#   one in stop mode with MAX_DUMPS 0, which only reports "still" and never takes a dump slot;
#   one in periodic mode, 15 dumps 20 s apart, which covers 40 s to 340 s around the freeze at
#   about 93 s.
#
# init waits for each line, so both watch lines go first.
/redwood/bin/lsprobe 60 &
/redwood/bin/lsprobe 300 &
/redwood/bin/framewatch 5 0 backboardd SpringBoard &
/redwood/bin/framewatch --every 20 --count 15 SpringBoard backboardd &
/redwood/bin/rwtouch wait 90 swipe 0.5 0.985 0.5 0.3 250 wait 10 button home wait 50
# framewatch has no start delay, and init starts each line when the previous one returns, so
# the wait above is what puts this watcher at about 150 s. The threshold is 2 s and there are
# six dumps: the round has a 3 s hole every 15 s from about 180 s, and a 5 s threshold never
# fires inside a 3 s hole. Starting late keeps the boot's own frameless stretch from spending
# the dumps on something that is not the hole.
/redwood/bin/framewatch 2 6 backboardd SpringBoard
